Keep the video when writing its MP4 tags fails

After recording, the camera edits the MP4 in place to add its cover and HDR boxes. Only an
IOException was caught there; any other exception ended the save and the video never reached
MediaStore. The handler, which logs and goes on without the tags, now catches every exception.

--- a/l4/D.smali
+++ b/l4/D.smali
@@ -691,7 +691,7 @@
 
     invoke-static {v9, v10}, Ltj/d;->a(Ljava/io/File;Ltj/b;)V
     :try_end_23a
-    .catch Ljava/io/IOException; {:try_start_232 .. :try_end_23a} :catch_23b
+    .catchall {:try_start_232 .. :try_end_23a} :catch_23b
 
     goto :goto_23f
 
